e Republican rollback of  broadband privacy protections now this  does still need to pass the house until  it's officially  made law and then of course Donald Trump  would also have to sign it but the point  is it's not too late to call your  elected officials on this this is an  obvious disgusting intrusion into our  privacy and it's a classic example Pat  of conservatives are blindly going with  their the the anti the the abandonment  of any regulation and they they push it  under the idea of over small government  we're talking about just basic people's  privacy here and this is a handout for  ISPs to make even more money they're  already gouging you on price and  providing subpar service now on top of  it they're gonna be able to make more  money by selling your your preference to  advertisers and I'm sure if you polled  the American public on that there would  be in wide support of keeping the Obama  era regulation absolutely absolutely  right  as long as some of them you wouldn't  want to tell them that it was an Obama  regulation you would just say are you in  favor of this rule and overwhelmingly  people would say absolutely at my  browsing history shouldn't be sold but  who would be in favor of this the ISPs  the Internet service providers companies  like Verizon AT&amp;T Comcast and those are  the people that not only fund the  campaigns for these congressmen and  Senators but also fund media outlets  like MSNBC and Fox News and the rest of  the cable outlets it's the whole  corporate media industrial complex and  everything that I've been telling you  about for years and how could a single  Republican not vote against this you  have to wonder what kind of money  changed hands here what kind of promises  were made behind the scenes for this to  pass there are people online saying if  the resolution passes we should create a  GoFundMe page so that we could buy the  internet browsing histories of the  senators who voted for this I don't know  that it'll exac